# Runs before every commit, and blocks it when either gate fails.
#
# Deliberately not the test suite: 106 tests cost 3 seconds today, but a hook that
# grows with the suite is how people end up committing with --no-verify, which
# makes the whole gate worthless. Lint and types are the two failures that cost
# the most to find later and the least to catch here.
#
# Tests run on demand (`pnpm test`). To skip this hook on purpose:
#   git commit --no-verify
#
# Husky runs this file through `sh -e`, so the first failure stops the commit.

pnpm lint
pnpm typecheck
